<title>FRANCE: Suez sees 3.5 bln Ffr profit in 1997.</title>
<headline>Suez sees 3.5 bln Ffr profit in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Groupe Suez Chairman Gerard Mestrallet confirmed on Wednesday that Suez/Lyonnaise, the new company formed by the merger of Suez and Lyonnaise des Eaux would earn a 1997 net profit of at least 3.5 billion francs.</p>
<p>&quot;We expect for 1997 more than 3.5 billion francs for the whole of the group, or about 28 francs per Lyonnaise share,&quot; Mestrallet told a shareholders' meeting.</p>
<p>He also repeated his hopes of doubling that in five years. He said that if the two companies had been merged on January 1, 1996 it would have earned about two billion francs last year.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
